# .trivyignore — the ONLY CVE escape hatch for the L4 security gate (Story 14.4 / ISI-2245, §6.2).
#
# This file is reviewed like code. Every suppression MUST carry, on the comment line directly
# above the CVE id:
#     <CVE-ID>   expires:YYYY-MM-DD   justification:<one line why this is accepted>
#
# The security.yml "trivyignore expiry lint" step FAILS the build when an entry is past its
# `expires:` date — a suppression is never a silent, perpetual mute. Remove or re-justify it
# before it expires. An unfixable finding still needs an entry (Trivy runs --ignore-unfixed, but
# a fix landing upstream turns a previously-unfixable HIGH into a gating one, so track it here).
#
# Format reference: https://trivy.dev/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/#trivyignore
#
# --- active suppressions ---
# openssl CVE batch in the ksquad-console RUNTIME base (gcr.io/distroless/nodejs24-debian12:nonroot,
# libssl3 3.0.18-1~deb12u2, debian 12.13). Fixes exist upstream (libssl3 3.0.19/3.0.20-1~deb12u2 in
# bookworm security) and ride the next distroless tag rebuild; distroless has no package manager so
# the image cannot be patched in-repo. Tracked by ISI-2852; remove these entries once the rebuilt
# base carries libssl3 >= 3.0.20.
# CVE-2026-31789   expires:2026-09-18   justification:CRITICAL openssl heap overflow (32-bit X.509); runtime-base-only, patch pending distroless rebuild of nodejs24-debian12
CVE-2026-31789
# CVE-2026-28387   expires:2026-09-18   justification:HIGH openssl DANE TLSA use-after-free; runtime-base-only, patch pending distroless rebuild of nodejs24-debian12
CVE-2026-28387
# CVE-2026-28388   expires:2026-09-18   justification:HIGH openssl delta-CMS NULL deref DoS; runtime-base-only, patch pending distroless rebuild of nodejs24-debian12
CVE-2026-28388
# CVE-2026-28389   expires:2026-09-18   justification:HIGH openssl CMS processing DoS; runtime-base-only, patch pending distroless rebuild of nodejs24-debian12
CVE-2026-28389
# CVE-2026-28390   expires:2026-09-18   justification:HIGH openssl CMS NULL deref DoS; runtime-base-only, patch pending distroless rebuild of nodejs24-debian12
CVE-2026-28390
# CVE-2026-45447   expires:2026-09-18   justification:HIGH openssl PKCS7_verify use-after-free; runtime-base-only, patch pending distroless rebuild of nodejs24-debian12
CVE-2026-45447

# --- ISI-3923: 2026-09 CVE batch surfaced by the Trivy DB across the toolchain images ---
# These are baked into UPSTREAM release binaries we download by pinned version (helm, kubectl,
# gh, dtctl, docker-cli) or bundled inside npm shipped in node:22-alpine — none are patchable in
# this repo, they clear only when the upstream tool ships a rebuild compiled with the fixed dep.
# All toolchain-image-only (no runtime/console exposure). Tracked by ISI-3923; a remediation
# follow-up bumps the pinned upstream versions / npm as patched releases land. Re-justify before
# expiry rather than blind-renew.
#
# Go stdlib / x-net advisories fixed in Go 1.26.6 — present in the helm v3.21.4 and kubectl
# v1.36.4 release binaries (compiled with Go 1.26.5). Download-only, not rebuildable in-repo.
# CVE-2026-33818   expires:2026-09-21   justification:HIGH Go encoding/asn1 DoS; upstream helm/kubectl binary compiled with Go 1.26.5, fix rides next release built on Go 1.26.6
CVE-2026-33818
# CVE-2026-39821   expires:2026-09-21   justification:HIGH Go net/http via x/net/idna; upstream helm/kubectl binary, fix rides next Go-1.26.6 release
CVE-2026-39821
# CVE-2026-46600   expires:2026-09-21   justification:HIGH Go x/net/dns/dnsmessage DoS; upstream helm/kubectl binary, fix rides next Go-1.26.6 release
CVE-2026-46600
# CVE-2026-56853   expires:2026-09-21   justification:HIGH Go net/http unencrypted HTTP/2; upstream helm/kubectl binary, fix rides next Go-1.26.6 release
CVE-2026-56853
# CVE-2026-56858   expires:2026-09-21   justification:HIGH Go html/template XSS; upstream helm/kubectl binary, fix rides next Go-1.26.6 release
CVE-2026-56858
# CVE-2026-56859   expires:2026-09-21   justification:HIGH Go encoding/xml DoS; upstream helm/kubectl binary, fix rides next Go-1.26.6 release
CVE-2026-56859
# CVE-2026-56860   expires:2026-09-21   justification:HIGH Go net/url DoS; upstream helm/kubectl binary, fix rides next Go-1.26.6 release
CVE-2026-56860
# CVE-2026-56862   expires:2026-09-21   justification:HIGH Go crypto/tls DoS; upstream helm/kubectl binary, fix rides next Go-1.26.6 release
CVE-2026-56862
#
# helm v3.21.4 binary vendored modules (fixes in x/crypto 0.55.0 / oras-go 2.6.2).
# CVE-2026-56854   expires:2026-09-21   justification:CRITICAL golang.org/x/crypto/ssh; vendored in upstream helm v3.21.4 binary (helm exposes no SSH server), fix rides next helm release
CVE-2026-56854
# CVE-2026-50163   expires:2026-09-21   justification:HIGH oras.land/oras-go/v2 info disclosure/arbitrary-file; vendored in upstream helm v3.21.4 binary, fix rides next helm release
CVE-2026-50163
#
# gh v2.98.0 binary vendored golang.org/x/mod (fix 0.40.0).
# CVE-2026-56864   expires:2026-09-21   justification:HIGH golang.org/x/mod malicious GOSUMDB arbitrary module; vendored in upstream gh v2.98.0 binary, fix rides next gh release
CVE-2026-56864
# CVE-2026-56865   expires:2026-09-21   justification:HIGH golang.org/x/mod/sumdb/tlog; vendored in upstream gh v2.98.0 binary, fix rides next gh release
CVE-2026-56865
#
# grpc-go (fix 1.83.1) vendored in the gh v2.98.0 and dtctl v0.38.0 upstream binaries.
# CVE-2026-84304   expires:2026-09-21   justification:HIGH google.golang.org/grpc; vendored in upstream gh v2.98.0 / dtctl v0.38.0 binaries, fix rides next upstream release
CVE-2026-84304
#
# docker:29-cli binary vendored github.com/moby/go-archive (fix 0.3.0).
# CVE-2026-17106   expires:2026-09-21   justification:HIGH github.com/moby/go-archive arbitrary-file; vendored in upstream docker:29-cli binary, fix rides next docker-cli release
CVE-2026-17106
#
# npm 12.0.2 bundled deps in the node:22-alpine toolchain image; patched versions ride a future
# npm release the node toolchain then re-pins (Dockerfile.toolchain-node NPM_VERSION, ISI-3444).
# CVE-2026-14257   expires:2026-09-21   justification:HIGH brace-expansion DoS (fix 5.0.8); bundled in npm 12.0.2, toolchain-image-only, rides next npm re-pin
CVE-2026-14257
# CVE-2026-69152   expires:2026-09-21   justification:HIGH brace-expansion DoS bypass of CVE-2026-14257 (fix 5.0.9); bundled in npm 12.0.2, toolchain-image-only, rides next npm re-pin
